    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0167" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157 SA 29/1834</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Attorney General</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jackson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-14">March 14, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have your letter of
                    March 13 and concur in the conclusion reached by your Legal Adviser that it is
                    legally unobjectionable so far as this country is concerned for the executives
                    of the United States and Canada to enter into an agreement regarding the Great
                    Lakes–St. Lawrence Deep Waterway project conditioned for its effectiveness upon
                    the subsequent enactment of necessary legislation by the Congress and by the
                    Canadian Parliament.</p>
                <p>If an agreement is executed and approved in this manner, its provisions would be
                    binding upon the United States as respects Canada.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Jackson</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
